**How to implement.** AT-1's build gains the experiments and their data (001 §Q AT-1 'Attach, split by `experiment`, match by the lab template. Roles for Darkness, BullshitCheck and the AIR repeats. The LR correction and the excluded frame are applied as data'; 001 §K; 001 §1a). `buildOpticsMuellerKit` (step 421) continues, through the window's messages alone. (1) The draft: `ActivateSetup` of `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `ExpChooseElement` of the Analyzer 1 slot, `ExpChooseVariable VaryDialReading` (0…360° over 19 points, offered because `LP2` is dial-mounted, step 289) and `ExpChooseMeasurement` of the capture the `Phone`'s slot offers: one experiment is one analyzer-dial sweep recorded as raw dial readings (001 §1a), every lab capture's description among those readings. (2) The data, file by file in this order: `data/raw/final/lp_lp.csv`, `data/raw/final/lp_cpl.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_lp.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day1_main.csv`, `data/raw/final/cpl_cpl_day2_corrections.csv`, `data/raw/final/darkness_checks.csv`, `data/raw/final/bullshit_checks.csv`. For each, `SplitByColumn (FileName <its absolute name inside the built folder>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)` (step 319: the Phone ROI CSV profile, `parseMuellerCsv`, split by `experiment`); `ToggleSplitOffer` of every group offered its setup and experiment by the template (step 318's rule (d): the forty grid setups hold every readable key); for the groups the template cannot read, `OfferSplitGroupOver` (step 422) over their family's AIR setup: `Darkness` over `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(Darkness)-CPL2` over `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `LP-(Darkness)-LP-2` and `-2R` over `LP-(AIR#0)-LP`, `CPL-(Darkness)-LP-2` and `-2R` and both `BullshitCheck` captures over `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP` (the family each was taken in, by its name or its time); then `MatchByTemplate`. Each file is attached in place (step 134: a file inside the kit is recorded, never copied), so the kit's 53 experiments are the 53 groups, named by their keys, each with `KeyedDataRows` of its key. (3) Roles (`SetExperimentRole`, step 294): `CalibrationRun` for the nine AIR runs `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2`, `LP-(AIR#0)-CPL-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-LP-2R`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-BR`, `CPL-(AIR#0)-CPL-2` (stage 1 calibrates on them and every session's gain anchors to them, 001 §L; a `DriftCheckRun` would be fitted as an object run by stage 2, step 385, which an AIR run cannot be), `DarkRun` for the six darkness captures, `DiagnosticRun` for `BullshitCheck` and `BullshitCheck-2`; every other experiment stays `ScienceRun`. (4) Sessions (`SetExperimentSession`, step 294; 001 §L 'Sessions and gain models as data … by hand'), the reference's six gain blocks (step 356): `LP-LP` for the eleven `lp_lp.csv` experiments, `LP-CPL` for the eleven `lp_cpl.csv` ones, `CPL-LP before the restart` for the `cpl_lp.csv` experiments whose captures all precede the earliest `BullshitCheck` capture (the laser restart that splits the CPL-LP gain block, 001 §1a; read from the data, not transcribed) and `CPL-LP after the restart` for the rest, `CPL-CPL day 1` and `CPL-CPL day 2` for the two `cpl_cpl` files' experiments; the darkness and diagnostic captures hold no session. (5) The LR correction, as data (001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact … with a mandatory audit note'): `CorrectSetup` (step 316) re-points `CPL-(LR#90)-CPL` to `CPL-(LR#-90)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#90)-CPL` to `CPL-(QZ#90-LR#-90)-CPL` (step 421), each with the note `LR was labelled +90 but physically sat at -90 (optics-mueller AGENTS.md, Current Known Caveats).`. The lab's caveat is the day-1 CPL-CPL dataset's; its `LR#45` runs were re-measured at +45 on day 2 (`CPL-(LR#45)-CPL-2`, `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL-2`; optics-mueller `notes/images_final_export_task.md:39-46`), so no `+45` run of the final data is re-pointed. The reference used +90 for these two runs; a Mueller rotation repeats every 180°, so −90° gives the same rotation and the reference values stay reproducible within `dataMatrixTol`. (6) The excluded frame, as data (001 §K 'exclusions carry a reason'): `ReviewExperimentData`, then `ExcludePoint` (step 315) of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2` at the `MappedPointNumber` of the point whose capture index is `MuellerReference.excludedPoints`' (17, at 140°; `BerremanTestSupport/MuellerReference.fs`, step 348), its place among the key's points in file order, with the reason `Likely contaminated frame; keep visible in plots but exclude from harmonic fits.` (`data/optics-mueller/data/reference/matrix_glue.py:27`). (7) The fact `AT-1 attaches every lab group of the final data files through the Phone ROI CSV profile, with its role, session, correction and exclusion`: after the build, a second `KitProxy.create` of the built folder reads exactly the 53 experiments, in the files' group order, each over the setup its key reads to (the darkness and diagnostic captures over the setups named in (2), the two corrected ones over their −90° setups with one `SetupCorrection` from their labelled setup carrying the note), with the dial-sweep scan, the role and session above, and `dataOpt` the attachment of its lab file at `data/raw/final/<file>` (the committed file's SHA-256), profile `Phone ROI CSV`, `KeyedDataRows` of its key and no exclusion but the one point of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`; each reads through the window's `experimentData` (`readMapped`, step 305) to its group's points, and `MappedPoints.keptBy` (step 314) of `LP-(LR#90)-CPL-2`'s keeps every point but the excluded one; and no file under `data/` is changed or added. The step-421 fact keeps its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After AT-1's second part lands, the build MUST attach every group of the seven final lab files in place through the Phone ROI CSV profile to an experiment named by its key, with the specified roles, sessions, LR correction and excluded frame, touching no lab file; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-1 attaches every lab group of the final data files through the Phone ROI CSV profile, with its role, session, correction and exclusion`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s41 invariants MUST pass.
